Test rg55a: literals with a blank under -a, numbered wrongly by the pool key
// Run with -a, so a blank adds.  The pool key's number takes a blank as OR, so where
// the terms share a bit, literals of different values once shared one pool word, and
// all but the first loaded a wrong value.  The comment on each line is the word its
// literal must load.
100/
    lac [3 1]           // 000004
    lac [3]             // 000003
    lac [4]             // 000004
    lac [lac 7 1]       // 200010
    lac [lac 7]         // 200007
    hlt
    constants
stop
